    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d226">

                <pb facs="0261" n="145" sameAs="frus:frus1912/pg145"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 893.51/989.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The American Minister to the Secretary of
                    State</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Legation</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Peking</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1912-07-09">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">July 9, 1912</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>The Premier and the Minister of Finance were informed this afternoon by the six
                    ministers of the instructions received from their several Governments. The reply
                    was that the acceptance of the terms of supervision were impossible; that the
                    National Council will not approve and public opinion will not permit.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Calhoun.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
